  "title": "Alder Lane",
  "problem": "During heavy rain events including storms and hurricanes, homeowners along Alder Lane, Dusenberry Road, Forest Lane, and Ridgecroft Road flood. Specifically, repetitive damage has occurred at 35 Alder Lane, 30 Forest Lane, 39 Dusenberry Road, 40 Dusenberry Road, 35 Ridgecroft Road.",
  "solution": "The Village has retained PCI Engineering to design plans which include new flood channels in existing open space between Middle Road and Crawford Street as well as between Grove Street and Crawford Street. The flood channel will then run parallel along Crawford Street where it is anticipated to tie into a new storm water line running within the Town of Eastchester. The Village is also exploring the feasibility of a storm water retention pond within Crawford Park which is owned by the Village of Bronxville. Finally, the Village is working with the Town of Eastchester to explore the feasibility of installing a new storm water line down Crawford Road which will run parralel to an existing, undersized line. The existing storm water line running down Dusenberry Road (which ties into the existing line on Crawford Street) will also be retrofitted with backflow devices to ensure it is not overwhelmed by surcharges elsewhere thereby allowing the storm water to flow out of the system. PCI is currently preparing drawings of the new systems.",
  "altAction": "Constructions of Flood Channels only",
  "altEval": "Alternative action was not selected as it would not resolve surcharges of stormwater system. The action would slow flooding in some areas but would not provide sufficient capacity without improvements to stormwater systems themselves.",
